{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "testhub-smoke-tests-v1",
    "name": "testHub — Smoke Tests",
    "description": "## Smoke Test Suites for testHub API\n\nTwo preconfigured test sequences to validate testHub after any deployment or code change.\n\n### 🟢 Quick Smoke  |  5 requests · ~30 seconds\n**When to run:** After frontend-only or infra changes, quick health check\n**What it tests:** All 3 services alive, auth working, DB connected, aggregation pipeline working\n\n**Requests:**\n1. Gateway Health Check\n2. Login - Admin (get fresh token)\n3. GET /api/auth/me (verify token round-trip)\n4. GET /api/projects (core-service + DB alive)\n5. GET /api/dashboard/stats (aggregation pipeline + new fields)\n\n### 🔵 Full Smoke  |  13 requests · ~2-3 minutes\n**When to run:** After any backend change, before pushing, full CRUD chain validation\n**What it tests:** Complete end-to-end flow: create project → suite → test case → run (with TC selection) → mark result → cleanup\n\n**Requests 1-5:** Same as Quick Smoke (services up, auth working)\n**Requests 6-13:** Full CRUD chain\n6. Create Project\n7. Create Suite\n8. Create Test Case\n9. Create Run (with testCaseIds selection)\n10. Get Run (verify TC filtering works)\n11. Update Run Status → COMPLETED\n12. Submit Result (PASS)\n13. Delete Project (cleanup + cascade)\n\n### Setup\n1. Update collection variables: `adminEmail`, `adminPassword` with your existing admin credentials\n2. Just run the folder — Login happens automatically in the first request\n3. Token auto-refresh is built in (pre-request script)\n\n### New Fields (Last Update)\n- `testCaseIds: []` — optional field when creating runs (test case selection feature)\n- `POST /api/runs/project/:projectId` now accepts `testCaseIds: [\"id1\", \"id2\", ...]` body\n- `GET /api/dashboard/stats` now returns `latestRunResults`, `latestRunName`, `latestRunStatus`\n\n### Import Instructions\n1. Open Postman → Collections → Import → choose this file\n2. Select or create an environment (can use same as Full Collection)\n3. Update `adminEmail` + `adminPassword` in collection variables\n4. Run either folder via Collection Runner or click \"Run Folder\"",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Auto-refresh accessToken when it expires within 60 seconds",
          "const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
          "const refresh = pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken');",
          "if (token && refresh) {",
          "    try {",
          "        const parts = token.split('.');",
          "        if (parts.length === 3) {",
          "            const payload = JSON.parse(atob(parts[1]));",
          "            const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
          "            if (payload.exp && payload.exp - now < 60) {",
          "                pm.sendRequest({",
          "                    url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/api/auth/refresh',",
          "                    method: 'POST',",
          "                    header: [{ key: 'Content-Type', value: 'application/json' }],",
          "                    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ refreshToken: refresh }) }",
          "                }, (err, res) => {",
          "                    if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
          "                        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', res.json().accessToken);",
          "                    }",
          "                });",
          "            }",
          "        }",
          "    } catch(e) {}",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl",        "value": "https://testhub-gateway.onrender.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken",    "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken",   "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail",     "value": "admin@testhub.com",  "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword",  "value": "admin123",           "type": "string" },
    { "key": "projectId",      "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "suiteId",        "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testCaseId",     "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "runId",          "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🟢 Quick Smoke  |  5 requests · ~30 sec",
      "description": "Fast health check after any change. Verifies all 3 services are up, auth works, and DB is connected. Run first before Full Smoke.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "[QS-1] Gateway Health Check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Gateway is alive', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Response time acceptable (cold start <60s)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(60000);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Hits gateway health. Use this to wake up free-tier services. Cold start ~24s."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[QS-2] Login - Admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has tokens', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('user', 'accessToken', 'refreshToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Save tokens to collection', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('✓ Tokens saved. Logged in as:', body.user.email);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in and saves tokens for subsequent requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[QS-3] Verify Token (GET /api/auth/me)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Returns current user', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('id', 'name', 'email', 'role');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.role).to.eql('ADMIN');",
                  "    console.log('✓ Token valid. User:', body.name, '(' + body.email + ')');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the bearer token is valid and round-tripping correctly."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[QS-4] List Projects (core-service alive)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response structure correct', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('items');",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('pagination');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('✓ core-service + DB alive. Total projects:', pm.response.json().pagination.total);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/projects?page=1&limit=10",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "projects"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page",  "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "10" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verifies core-service is up and DB is connected."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[QS-5] Dashboard Stats (new fields check)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has all required stat fields', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys(",
                  "        'totalProjects', 'activeProjects', 'totalTestCases',",
                  "        'totalRuns', 'activeRuns', 'passRatePercent',",
                  "        'recentRuns', 'resultBreakdown',",
                  "        'latestRunResults', 'latestRunName', 'latestRunStatus'",
                  "    );",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Stats are numeric', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.totalProjects).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.passRatePercent).to.be.within(0, 100);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Result breakdown has PASS/FAIL/SKIP/BLOCKED', () => {",
                  "    const bd = pm.response.json().resultBreakdown;",
                  "    pm.expect(bd).to.have.all.keys('PASS', 'FAIL', 'SKIP', 'BLOCKED');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('New fields: latestRunResults, latestRunName, latestRunStatus', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.latestRunResults).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    pm.expect([null, 'string']).to.include(typeof body.latestRunName);",
                  "    console.log('✓ Dashboard aggregation working. Pass rate:', body.passRatePercent + '%');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/stats",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "dashboard", "stats"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies dashboard aggregation pipeline works and checks for new fields (latestRunResults, latestRunName, latestRunStatus)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
